[ AWS ECR login info and (possibly) docker image refresh service ]

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
If you change...            | Run this command          | Why?
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The script code (.sh file)  | Nothing                   | The service reads the file from disk every time it starts.
The Service file (.service) | systemctl daemon-reload   | To tell systemd to look at the new configuration file.
The Timer file (.timer)     | systemctl daemon-reload   | To update the frequency (e.g., changing 8h to 4h).
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------


* Source codes for AWS ECR login info refresh service: 
/etc/systemd/system/ecr-refresh.timer : Periodically launches ecr-refresh.service
/etc/systemd/system/ecr-refresh.service : Runs ecr-refresh-update.sh
/etc/systemd/system/ecr-refresh.service.d/override.conf : Set the env variable so that the aws uses credentials and config file under /home/cym/.aws
                                                         (Edit by $ sudo systemctl edit ecr-refresh.service)
/usr/local/bin/ecr-refresh-update.sh : Actual script for the periodic ecr-refresh service 
                                      (manual force update : $sudo /usr/local/bin/ecr-refresh-update.sh)


* Manually start the timer service:
$ sudo systemctl daemon-reload
$ sudo systemctl enable --now ecr-refresh.timer 

* Manually re-start the timer service when either .service or .timer file is updated:
$ sudo systemctl daemon-reload
$ sudo systemctl restart ecr-refresh.timer 

